and Huang Ji Huang concepts. The company also offers online food delivery services. Yum China Holdings, Inc. was founded in 1987 and is headquartered in Shanghai, the People's Republic of China.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Joey  Wat | CEO & Executive Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $8.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 130K people. Revenue per employee of $91K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 6%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $6K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $323 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 98\u00d7 revenue per employee (high relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Yum China Holdings, Inc. is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $16.8B market cap on $11.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 23% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 15-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $840M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.58\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 8.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 27% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Analysts Have Made A Financial Statement On Yum China Holdings, Inc.'s (NYSE:YUMC) Third-Quarter Report","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/consumer-services/nyse-yumc/yum-china-holdings/news/analysts-have-made-a-financial-statement-on-yum-china-holdin","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793963443.56,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.859,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Here's Why Yum China Holdings (YUMC) is a Strong Value Stock